WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:18.914
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:19.184 --> 01:20.727
Found it.

3
01:28.568 --> 01:31.154
Great. Thanks for your hard work. I'll be there soon.

4
01:31.654 --> 01:33.406
-Hang tight. -Okay.

5
01:33.489 --> 01:36.034
He killed them here, then moved them to a freezer.

6
01:40.705 --> 01:42.582
But there's no sign of the tiger.

7
01:43.124 --> 01:45.919
That's okay. You said there's a cage.

8
01:46.002 --> 01:47.420
I'll put out another APB now.

9
01:48.129 --> 01:50.632
It looks like he's been working on something.

10
01:52.884 --> 01:54.260
A stage?

11
01:56.971 --> 01:58.181
What's this?

12
02:10.151 --> 02:11.236
There's a note.

13
02:13.571 --> 02:14.697
It's in Hangeul.

14
02:15.782 --> 02:18.618
-I'll send you a picture. -Okay, I'll check it out now.

15
02:34.092 --> 02:35.134
Hello?

16
02:35.635 --> 02:36.594
Hello?

17
02:37.637 --> 02:40.390
I'm sorry. I'll call you back.

18
02:44.519 --> 02:45.561
What's up with him?

19
02:50.608 --> 02:52.110
Kim Seok.

20
02:54.320 --> 02:56.239
Detective Kim Seok.

21
02:59.867 --> 03:01.202
SEOUL POLICE KIM SEOK'S MOTHER

22
03:01.286 --> 03:02.453
Kim Seok?

23
03:02.537 --> 03:04.122
MARIA NURSING HOME

24
03:57.925 --> 04:00.887
THE BLUE ROAD

25
04:04.682 --> 04:05.975
Please help me.

26
04:06.809 --> 04:08.353
Please help me.

27
04:09.062 --> 04:09.979
Please.

28
04:17.945 --> 04:18.946
What happened exactly?

29
04:19.030 --> 04:21.908
A young man came to visit your mother and took her with him.

30
04:21.991 --> 04:23.701
He was Japanese.

31
04:25.328 --> 04:26.954
We've been looking for her, but…

32
04:29.499 --> 04:31.292
Ms. Lee Ae-gyeong!

33
04:32.293 --> 04:34.045
-Are you okay? -Where are you?

34
04:34.712 --> 04:36.214
Ms. Lee, where are you?

35
04:36.297 --> 04:37.215
Where are you?

36
04:37.298 --> 04:38.800
Ms. Lee Ae-gyeong!

37
04:38.883 --> 04:40.676
Can you hear my voice?

38
04:40.760 --> 04:42.595
Where are you?

39
04:43.304 --> 04:44.764
Ms. Lee Ae-gyeong!

40
04:45.723 --> 04:47.975
-Where are you? -Can you hear us?

41
04:48.059 --> 04:50.186
Ms. Lee Ae-gyeong!

42
04:51.062 --> 04:52.271
Where are you?

43
04:52.355 --> 04:54.190
Ms. Lee Ae-gyeong!

44
05:19.006 --> 05:20.007
Mom!

45
05:23.428 --> 05:24.637
Mom!

46
05:27.056 --> 05:31.561
Mom!

47
05:36.190 --> 05:37.024
Mom.

48
05:42.947 --> 05:44.615
Don't move. Stay right there.

49
05:47.118 --> 05:48.077
It's dangerous.

50
05:49.787 --> 05:50.997
Mother.

51
05:52.957 --> 05:53.833
Who am I?

52
06:08.473 --> 06:09.724
Are you hurt?

53
06:09.807 --> 06:11.184
Who are you?

54
06:14.103 --> 06:15.521
Mom, it's me. Seok.

55
06:18.149 --> 06:19.817
Mom!

56
06:19.901 --> 06:21.652
-Get away from me, bastard! -Mother!

57
06:21.736 --> 06:23.029
Get away!

58
06:23.112 --> 06:24.780
-Mom! It's me, Seok! -Let go of me!

59
06:24.864 --> 06:26.824
-Get away from me, you bastard! -Mom!

60
06:27.492 --> 06:30.286
-You worthless bastard. Get away! -Mother!

61
06:30.786 --> 06:32.455
-You're okay. -Go away, you bastard!

62
06:33.039 --> 06:34.040
Mother!

63
06:35.041 --> 06:36.000
Are you okay?

64
06:36.083 --> 06:37.418
Is she okay?

65
06:38.127 --> 06:39.253
Inose…

66
06:43.508 --> 06:45.051
And who are you?

67
06:46.344 --> 06:48.679
Who the hell are you?

68
06:49.472 --> 06:50.598
Hello.

69
06:52.558 --> 06:54.519
My name is Inose Hiroshi.

70
06:55.561 --> 06:57.313
I'm a friend of Detective Kim's.

71
06:58.523 --> 07:00.900
How dare you, you Japanese bastard!

72
07:01.400 --> 07:04.445
My husband!

73
07:04.529 --> 07:05.655
You killed him.

74
07:05.738 --> 07:08.908
You Japanese bastards killed my husband!

75
07:08.991 --> 07:11.244
Get out. Can't you hear me?

76
07:11.327 --> 07:13.955
Get out of here, you Japanese bastards!

77
07:14.038 --> 07:17.166
Seok, your uncle.

78
07:17.250 --> 07:18.918
Where's Uncle Du-yeong?

79
07:19.001 --> 07:21.087
Seok. Where's Uncle Du-yeong?

80
07:21.170 --> 07:23.005
-It's okay. -Seok.

81
07:25.049 --> 07:26.300
Du-yeong.

82
07:26.384 --> 07:32.765
Du-yeong!

83
07:33.474 --> 07:34.308
Du-yeong…

84
07:52.118 --> 07:53.744
She has Alzheimer's.

85
07:55.788 --> 07:57.123
She's had it for a while.

86
08:04.964 --> 08:06.674
She wasn't in her right mind,

87
08:06.757 --> 08:09.135
so please don't take what she said to heart.

88
08:11.596 --> 08:12.972
I'm truly sorry.

89
08:15.850 --> 08:18.060
It's fine. No biggie.

90
08:18.644 --> 08:20.938
I couldn't understand anything anyway.

91
08:25.276 --> 08:26.611
My mother…

92
08:28.863 --> 08:30.823
was a mudang who served the gods.

93
08:32.408 --> 08:35.161
A Korean shaman.

94
08:43.836 --> 08:45.463
People were afraid of her.

95
08:49.717 --> 08:51.177
And so was I.

96
08:59.226 --> 09:00.353
And your father?

97
09:01.479 --> 09:03.731
His work was similar to my mother's.

98
09:05.358 --> 09:06.734
He was a geomancer.

99
09:08.527 --> 09:10.404
He traveled the country

100
09:10.488 --> 09:13.616
digging up iron stakes the Japanese buried during their occupation.

101
09:14.825 --> 09:18.412
Digging out those iron stakes that had been buried for decades.

102
09:19.955 --> 09:22.375
So, an anti-Japanese campaign of sorts.

103
09:23.292 --> 09:24.377
But then,

104
09:25.127 --> 09:27.046
he went missing.

105
09:29.632 --> 09:31.801
We don't even know if he's dead or alive.

106
09:32.635 --> 09:35.930
After that, I grew up under my uncle's care.

107
09:37.473 --> 09:39.308
The man my mom was calling for earlier.

108
09:40.685 --> 09:44.063
Saying, "Du-yeong!"

109
09:48.067 --> 09:51.320
He'd sought out my mother to learn the trade.

110
09:53.656 --> 09:56.325
Before long, he filled the void my father had left behind.

111
10:05.251 --> 10:06.961
And where is this uncle now?

112
10:12.216 --> 10:13.592
He died.

113
10:17.012 --> 10:20.850
That's when my mother's condition started to worsen.

114
10:24.145 --> 10:26.564
I fear I may have overshared.

115
10:28.357 --> 10:29.442
I'm sorry.

116
10:35.197 --> 10:36.657
Thank you

117
10:38.325 --> 10:39.160
for telling me.

118
10:43.622 --> 10:45.207
But what matters to us…

119
10:47.835 --> 10:50.880
is catching this pesky culprit.

120
10:59.638 --> 11:02.308
The hallway of the nursing home had a security camera.

121
11:02.808 --> 11:03.642
As you can see,

122
11:04.310 --> 11:06.395
it's like the bastard wanted to be filmed.

123
11:06.896 --> 11:08.773
He wanted us to see.

124
11:09.732 --> 11:12.318
But how did he know your mother was there?

125
11:12.818 --> 11:16.238
He's a clever bastard, who even used his detention to his advantage.

126
11:16.322 --> 11:19.742
It can't have been hard to get the hospital address from a neighbor.

127
11:22.077 --> 11:23.329
He's toying with us.

128
11:24.580 --> 11:26.081
While flaunting himself.

129
11:30.669 --> 11:32.838
The sly motherfucker.

130
11:33.339 --> 11:35.090
Hold on.

131
11:36.675 --> 11:37.885
Zoom in on this.

132
11:37.968 --> 11:39.512
-Zoom in? -Yes.

133
11:43.766 --> 11:45.392
What is this bastard saying?

134
11:45.893 --> 11:47.019
Re…

135
11:47.728 --> 11:48.562
Rehear…

136
11:48.646 --> 11:50.272
Rehearsal?

137
11:51.565 --> 11:52.608
Rehearsal?

138
11:53.901 --> 11:55.027
In other words,

139
11:55.778 --> 11:58.489
him going to see your mother was just a rehearsal?

140
11:58.572 --> 12:00.074
So he's preparing for something?

141
12:00.157 --> 12:02.117
What are you three cooking up this time?

142
12:02.201 --> 12:04.745
You lunatic. Well? What is it now?

143
12:04.829 --> 12:06.747
-We're checking the footage-- -Don't.

144
12:07.248 --> 12:08.415
Not a word.

145
12:08.916 --> 12:11.752
No good ever fucking comes from getting mixed up with you lot.

146
12:12.253 --> 12:14.213
I'm starving. What are we eating?

147
12:20.928 --> 12:22.096
What is this?

148
12:24.306 --> 12:25.349
What's wrong?

149
12:26.600 --> 12:28.060
There's no way.

150
12:28.602 --> 12:29.687
URGENT NOTICE

151
12:29.770 --> 12:32.273
LEE HYEON-SEO, PATIENT UNDER POLICE SUPERVISION, MISSING

152
12:32.356 --> 12:37.361
Okay, everyone. Let's all practice how we'll cheer!

153
12:37.862 --> 12:41.156
Do you all know the cheer that's on TV everywhere these days?

154
12:41.240 --> 12:44.326
The one where you clap five times. You know the drill, right?

155
12:44.410 --> 12:45.578
Let's give it a go.

156
12:47.329 --> 12:49.540
Republic of Korea!

157
12:50.666 --> 12:51.876
Republic of Korea!

158
12:51.959 --> 12:54.503
Hold on. Today's our first game, everyone.

159
12:54.587 --> 12:57.214
We need to give it everything we've got. What do we say?

160
12:57.298 --> 12:59.091
Republic of Korea!

161
13:00.885 --> 13:03.053
Republic of Korea!

162
13:04.096 --> 13:06.390
Republic of Korea!

163
13:13.188 --> 13:14.857
What about the officers there?

164
13:18.903 --> 13:21.614
All personnel were deployed to City Hall and Gwanghwamun

165
13:21.697 --> 13:23.532
due to the World Cup cheering events.

166
13:24.158 --> 13:26.035
This is why he called it a rehearsal.

167
13:26.869 --> 13:28.329
Hyeon-seo is the main event.

168
13:30.205 --> 13:31.916
To the hospital. Now!

169
13:31.999 --> 13:34.293
We move fast but quietly. Got it?

170
13:34.376 --> 13:36.337
-We don't have time. Move! -Lead team, go.

171
13:36.420 --> 13:37.338
Yes, sir!

172
13:40.549 --> 13:42.468
Let's make this a public investigation.

173
13:42.551 --> 13:43.844
-We need to hurry. -Move.

174
13:43.928 --> 13:46.013
-For fuck's sake! -You little shit!

175
13:46.931 --> 13:48.307
Forgot your place?

176
13:48.390 --> 13:51.060
The vehicle, the composite sketch, or the sighting on CCTV.

177
13:51.143 --> 13:53.145
We don't have time to get this to the press.

178
13:53.228 --> 13:56.190
So you want to advertise that a crazy killer is on the loose?

179
13:57.775 --> 13:59.902
It's so we can catch him.

180
14:01.278 --> 14:03.030
The boss said no.

181
14:03.781 --> 14:05.449
Because of the World Cup.

182
14:11.664 --> 14:12.873
Start the car.

183
14:17.294 --> 14:18.629
Calm down.

184
14:19.171 --> 14:21.173
Deep breaths.

185
14:26.387 --> 14:27.429
First, the hospital--

186
14:27.513 --> 14:29.515
No. Then it'll be too late.

187
14:29.598 --> 14:32.351
-So what do you suggest? -We need to think.

188
14:41.026 --> 14:42.945
Emi is an artist.

189
14:43.028 --> 14:45.280
A perfectionist who constantly craves approval.

190
14:45.823 --> 14:49.618
That's why he hasn't slipped up once.

191
14:53.163 --> 14:54.248
Could it be?

192
14:56.750 --> 14:58.377
You could come to my upcoming show.

193
14:58.877 --> 15:02.006
This time, it'll be an interactive sound art piece…

194
15:02.089 --> 15:05.259
During his interrogation, he said I should come see his show.

195
15:05.843 --> 15:07.386
He said it would be interactive.

196
15:10.055 --> 15:10.931
Rehearsal.

197
15:14.393 --> 15:17.229
With a bit of a performance element too.

198
15:17.312 --> 15:18.564
A performance.

199
15:20.983 --> 15:21.900
That's it.

200
15:22.401 --> 15:24.695
I was wondering what he meant back then.

201
15:24.778 --> 15:27.197
One second. Could you take a look at this?

202
15:28.365 --> 15:31.243
It says Emi Shunsuke is giving a piano performance in Gunsan today.

203
15:31.326 --> 15:33.037
SPECIAL PRE-WORLD CUP PERFORMANCE PIANIST EMI SHUNSUKE

204
15:35.122 --> 15:36.206
Gunsan.

205
15:36.915 --> 15:37.750
Yeah.

206
15:38.250 --> 15:40.586
Request backup from the Gunsan Police now.

207
15:40.669 --> 15:41.795
Yes, sir.

208
15:48.719 --> 15:49.845
Republic of Korea!

209
15:49.928 --> 15:51.930
SPECIAL PRE-MATCH PERFORMANCE BY PIANIST EMI SHUNSUKE

210
16:00.230 --> 16:03.525
THE PERFORMANCE WILL BEGIN SHORTLY PLEASE TAKE YOUR SEATS

211
16:03.609 --> 16:05.903
The South Gunsan Police aren't very keen to help.

212
16:05.986 --> 16:07.362
With what happened last time--

213
16:07.446 --> 16:10.115
I didn't leave you there for nothing! Keep calling them.

214
16:11.867 --> 16:12.701
Hey.

215
17:11.301 --> 17:13.137
You woke up earlier than I expected.

216
17:14.429 --> 17:18.058
I even used more anesthetic this time.

217
17:28.527 --> 17:29.862
You

218
17:31.155 --> 17:33.448
will become the greatest instrument.

219
17:36.535 --> 17:39.621
An instrument that will live on in everyone's memories forever.

220
17:45.711 --> 17:47.796
Republic of Korea!

221
17:48.922 --> 17:50.674
Hello, viewers.

222
17:50.757 --> 17:53.093
At last, the day we've all been waiting for.

223
17:53.760 --> 17:58.265
Mr. Commentator, the atmosphere in and around the stadium is wild.

224
17:58.348 --> 18:03.645
The fans are cheering so loudly that my own voice is being drowned out.

225
18:07.107 --> 18:08.817
What the…

226
18:08.901 --> 18:10.527
Oh my gosh!

227
18:54.738 --> 18:57.658
Republic of Korea!

228
19:05.374 --> 19:07.918
Republic of Korea!

229
19:21.515 --> 19:24.518
Oh, victory Korea

230
19:24.601 --> 19:28.188
Oh, victory Korea

231
19:28.272 --> 19:31.650
Oh, olé, olé…

232
19:43.620 --> 19:44.788
We save Hyeon-seo first.

233
19:51.044 --> 19:52.170
A lift.

234
19:54.840 --> 19:57.092
It was a stage lift.

235
19:59.720 --> 20:01.346
The tiger was there.

236
20:02.347 --> 20:03.473
A lift?

237
20:15.652 --> 20:16.570
The mechanical room. Here.

238
20:22.534 --> 20:24.619
Inose! Another door!

239
20:53.023 --> 20:53.940
Let's go.

240
21:00.822 --> 21:02.240
It's okay.

241
21:02.324 --> 21:04.117
-Wait. -You're okay.

242
21:05.744 --> 21:07.496
Look. We're the police.

243
21:09.373 --> 21:10.415
Are you okay?

244
21:14.836 --> 21:15.879
Emi Shunsuke did this?

245
21:18.632 --> 21:19.549
Emi?

246
21:22.552 --> 21:27.057
That bastard came backstage, then he suddenly dragged me away.

247
21:28.725 --> 21:31.561
And then he brought this girl

248
21:32.062 --> 21:33.188
and a tiger…

249
22:00.382 --> 22:01.466
Thank you.

250
22:02.050 --> 22:05.053
I will now present my encore

251
22:05.554 --> 22:09.724
and the final exhibition of my life.

252
22:13.145 --> 22:14.312
Its title is…

253
22:15.313 --> 22:17.274
He said he'd let us hear it live.

254
22:18.775 --> 22:19.860
"Live."

255
22:20.360 --> 22:22.237
It's a message.

256
22:23.405 --> 22:25.866
He intends to plant fear into the audience.

257
22:25.949 --> 22:29.828
"One fear breeds infinite fear and all methods shall be concealed."

258
22:38.962 --> 22:41.631
He intends to showcase the moment of Hyeon-seo's death.

259
22:44.384 --> 22:47.304
Is there a lift room here, used for stage effects?

260
22:52.058 --> 22:53.185
There it is.

261
22:55.645 --> 22:56.646
The tiger.

262
23:56.498 --> 23:57.541
Hyeon-seo!

263
24:54.806 --> 24:56.891
Please…

264
24:58.935 --> 24:59.894
Please.

265
25:01.062 --> 25:01.938
Wake up.

266
25:02.439 --> 25:03.607
Please wake up.

267
25:03.690 --> 25:04.566
Hey, Inose.

268
25:09.654 --> 25:10.488
Hey.

269
25:12.699 --> 25:13.700
What's going on?

270
25:29.341 --> 25:31.926
The detective from back then.

271
25:41.728 --> 25:44.356
Now she won't make any sound.

272
26:35.281 --> 26:36.741
Emi Shunsuke!

273
27:39.012 --> 27:40.346
That's enough. Come out now.

274
27:42.140 --> 27:43.141
Now!

275
27:45.518 --> 27:47.937
Are you sure you even want to catch me?

276
27:49.898 --> 27:52.192
Then why do you look so conflicted?

277
27:53.651 --> 27:55.862
You should be focusing on me.

278
29:34.752 --> 29:36.337
That's got to hurt.

279
30:03.698 --> 30:05.366
You having fun?

280
30:07.911 --> 30:09.078
Because…

281
30:13.833 --> 30:14.959
I still got to…

282
30:16.711 --> 30:18.838
show my performance to the two people…

283
30:21.215 --> 30:22.759
I most wanted to show it to.

284
30:24.344 --> 30:27.138
You've been infected with fear.

285
30:34.854 --> 30:37.315
Stop! Hey, Inose!

286
30:42.403 --> 30:44.697
Feel that same pain yourself.

287
30:49.827 --> 30:51.955
Hey, Inose.

288
30:52.705 --> 30:53.706
Stop!

289
30:54.499 --> 30:55.333
Let go of me!

290
30:55.416 --> 30:57.168
That's enough. Stop it now.

291
31:03.341 --> 31:04.759
Are you okay?

292
31:04.842 --> 31:05.677
Inose.

293
31:08.137 --> 31:09.639
That's enough now.

294
31:10.181 --> 31:11.140
Okay?

295
31:11.641 --> 31:12.850
Let's arrest him now.

296
31:34.205 --> 31:35.248
No! Hey!

297
31:41.462 --> 31:43.172
If I die,

298
31:44.007 --> 31:45.133
would that be more fun?

299
31:48.386 --> 31:49.429
I'm sure

300
31:50.388 --> 31:53.099
you still have so many questions.

301
31:55.768 --> 31:57.103
The original…

302
32:08.197 --> 32:09.490
lives.

303
32:28.259 --> 32:29.677
Inose, snap out of it!

304
32:29.761 --> 32:31.137
Inose, hurry!

305
32:31.220 --> 32:33.181
The body from back then…

306
32:35.308 --> 32:36.601
Hong Du-yeong?

307
34:08.943 --> 34:10.653
URGENT NOTICE

308
34:10.736 --> 34:13.239
EMI SHUNSUKE PRONOUNCED DEAD DURING TRANSPORT

309
34:57.491 --> 34:58.701
Seok.

310
35:02.330 --> 35:03.956
Seok!

311
35:10.421 --> 35:11.964
Kim Seok!

312
36:04.058 --> 36:05.768
INOSE HIROSHI

313
36:07.228 --> 36:08.604
KIM…

314
36:13.359 --> 36:18.531
THE LATE LEE HYEON-SEO

315
36:33.421 --> 36:36.674
She was too young to have a resident registration card.

316
36:39.051 --> 36:40.678
So she doesn't have a photo.

317
36:58.404 --> 36:59.613
We failed

318
37:00.573 --> 37:01.949
to keep our promise.

319
37:28.601 --> 37:29.977
I guess this is it.

320
37:34.482 --> 37:36.400
Is it really over now?

321
37:54.960 --> 37:56.253
It was good working with you.

322
38:03.928 --> 38:05.971
Why did you let go of Emi's hand?

323
38:09.642 --> 38:10.976
My hand slipped.

324
38:16.107 --> 38:17.650
I believe I told you before…

325
38:20.528 --> 38:22.488
I really don't like people who keep secrets.

326
38:32.665 --> 38:33.666
Hong Du-yeong!

327
38:43.217 --> 38:44.969
The uncle I told you about before.

328
38:46.178 --> 38:47.179
Hong Du-yeong.

329
38:53.394 --> 38:54.603
He was a victim.

330
39:02.945 --> 39:04.989
The serial murder case in the '80s.

331
39:09.743 --> 39:11.245
The original…

332
39:13.539 --> 39:14.748
lives.

333
39:32.016 --> 39:33.476
In 2002,

334
39:34.852 --> 39:38.230
there was Emi Shunsuke, a serial murderer who contorted his victims' limbs…

335
39:40.107 --> 39:41.734
And the original from 1987,

336
39:41.817 --> 39:45.529
the serial murderer who twisted Hong Du-yeong's limbs…

337
39:48.824 --> 39:50.367
is yet to be caught.

338
43:49.982 --> 43:54.361
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
